49.7339,-123.1347],[49.7748,-123.1395],[49.8109,-123.1214],[49.8673,-123.1611],[49.941,-123.1678],[50.0154,-123.1233],[50.0499,-123.1253],[50.0778,-123.0858],[50.09,-122.9987],[50.1019,-122.9901],[50.1163,-122.9574]]}],"chat":{"alaska":{"title":"Alaska","notes":[{"need":"road","label":"Road","when":"2026-06-12","placeLabel":"Fairbanks","text":"The shoulder south of Fairbanks on the Richardson Highway was wide enough for a loaded bike in dry weather."},{"need":"water","label":"Water","when":"2026-06-25","placeLabel":"Delta Junction","text":"Filled every bottle at the visitor centre tap in Delta Junction. The next tap we trusted was in Tok, 175 km on."},{"need":"resupply","label":"Resupply","when":"2026-06-27","placeLabel":"Tok","text":"The grocery in Tok was well stocked. It was our last big shop before Whitehorse."},{"need":"border","label":"Border","when":"2024-08-14","placeLabel":"Port Alcan","text":"At Port Alcan customs asked for proof of funds and an onward ticket before letting us into Canada."},{"need":"stay","label":"Stay","when":"2026-06-10","placeLabel":"Fairbanks","text":"Camped two nights at a private campground on the edge of Fairbanks. Showers were coin-operated and the laundry worked."},{"need":"road","label":"Road","when":"2025-08-30","placeLabel":"Tok","text":"Frost heaves on the Alaska Highway east of Tok were bad enough to rattle bottles out of cages."},{"need":"safety","label":"Safety","when":"2026-07-01","placeLabel":"Delta Junction","text":"Saw a moose cow with a calf on the shoulder north of Delta Junction. We waited ten minutes for them to move off."},{"need":"season","label":"Season","when":"2026-06-05","placeLabel":"Fairbanks","text":"Midnight sun in early June: we rode late and slept with eye masks."},{"need":"water","label":"Water","when":"2026-07-03","placeLabel":"Northway","text":"No tap at the Northway turnoff when we passed. We filtered from a creek about 10 km east."}]},"yukon":{"title":"Yukon","notes":[{"need":"road","label":"Road","when":"2026-07-15","placeLabel":"Beaver Creek","text":"Mucha construcción entre Beaver Creek y Destruction Bay: tramos de grava suelta y esperamos al coche piloto unos 20 minutos."},{"need":"stay","label":"Stay","when":"2026-09-03","placeLabel":"Whitehorse","text":"The city campground in Whitehorse had closed for the season after Labour Day. The rec centre let us pitch tents on the grass for one night."},{"need":"safety","label":"Safety","when":"2026-06-20","placeLabel":"Haines Junction","text":"The food lockers at the Kluane rest stop were working and in use. We kept everything with a smell in them overnight."},{"need":"season","label":"Season","when":"2026-08-28","placeLabel":"Haines Junction","text":"First frost near Kluane at the end of August, and riders reported snow on the passes by mid-September."},{"need":"water","label":"Water","when":"2026-07-17","placeLabel":"Destruction Bay","text":"The lodge in Destruction Bay filled our bottles for free and asked us to buy a coffee."},{"need":"resupply","label":"Resupply","when":"2026-07-20","placeLabel":"Haines Junction","text":"Haines Junction had a small grocery with fresh fruit and fuel canisters, closed on Sunday afternoon."},{"need":"border","label":"Border","when":"2026-07-14","placeLabel":"Beaver Creek","text":"Canadian customs at Beaver Creek asked where we would camp and how long we would stay. About fifteen minutes in total."},{"need":"stay","label":"Stay","when":"2026-07-22","placeLabel":"Teslin","text":"Free camping by the Teslin bridge was quiet, but the outhouse was locked."},{"need":"road","label":"Road","when":"2026-08-02","placeLabel":"Watson Lake","text":"Fresh chip seal west of Watson Lake for about 30 km. Sharp gravel, two flats in the group."}]},"northern-bc":{"title":"Northern British Columbia","notes":[{"need":"road","label":"Road","when":"2026-07-28","placeLabel":"Dease Lake","text":"Paved all the way on the Cassiar Highway north of Dease Lake, but no shoulder and logging trucks in the morning."},{"need":"resupply","label":"Resupply","when":"2026-07-29","placeLabel":"Dease Lake","text":"Dease Lake has the only real grocery for a long stretch. Stock up for at least four days."},{"need":"water","label":"Water","when":"2026-07-30","placeLabel":"Iskut","text":"Iskut store sells water by the jug. Creeks south of town looked clean but we filtered."},{"need":"safety","label":"Safety","when":"2026-07-31","placeLabel":"Meziadin Junction","text":"Black bear crossed the road twice near Meziadin Junction. Cooked and stored food well away from the tents."},{"need":"stay","label":"Stay","when":"2026-08-04","placeLabel":"Liard River","text":"Camped at the hot springs campground at Liard River. Book ahead in summer, it was full by 5 pm."},{"need":"season","label":"Season","when":"2026-08-20","placeLabel":"Muncho Lake","text":"Cold rain for three days around Muncho Lake in late August. Wool layers saved us."},{"need":"border","label":"Border","when":"2026-08-25","placeLabel":"Stewart","text":"Riding into Hyder from Stewart there was no US check going in, but Canada checks passports coming back."}]},"southern-bc":{"title":"Southern British Columbia","notes":[{"need":"resupply","label":"Resupply","when":"2026-07-09","placeLabel":"Vancouver","text":"A grocery near the Vancouver start had bike boxes and ordinary food, nothing specialty."},{"need":"road","label":"Road","when":"2026-08-12","placeLabel":"Hope","text":"Highway 1 into Hope has a wide shoulder but heavy truck traffic on weekends."},{"need":"stay","label":"Stay","when":"2026-08-14","placeLabel":"Whistler","text":"Campsites near Whistler were booked out on a Saturday. A host from a cycling hospitality site took us in."},{"need":"water","label":"Water","when":"2026-08-10","placeLabel":"Cache Creek","text":"Hot and dry around Cache Creek. Gas stations were the only water stops for 80 km."},{"need":"season","label":"Season","when":"2026-08-08","placeLabel":"Williams Lake","text":"Wildfire smoke near Williams Lake in early August. We checked the provincial fire map every morning."},{"need":"safety","label":"Safety","when":"2026-08-16","placeLabel":"Vancouver","text":"Bike theft is common in Vancouver. Use two locks and bring panniers inside."}]}},"simulated":true,"roadShapes":"Highway shapes from OpenStreetMap via the OSRM demo router, fetched once. Display only; stage distances stay straight-line."}